// rustc borrowck/mut-borrow-conflict-in-closures-vec.rs — upstream E0499
// imported batch B167 @ da5114692c9ebe46b869488c5f34f92eb10b98c1 (rust 1.100.0)
// shelf: admit · root bck.NEW-CAPLOAN — RE-PORTED AS-IS 2026-09-07 (stage 4)
// Modifications:
//   · `RefCell::new(vec![])` -> a plain `Vec`; the `RefCell` is upstream's way of
//     pushing through a `&self` and is not the subject (its `ufcs()` twin is a separate
//     annotated site and a separate port)
//   · the slot type is written out and bounded `+ '_` per the 2026-09-02y split above
//   · assert -> exit code: `fn main() -> i32`
// ── BUCKET 2: re-ported as-is, still admitted, still a defect. The port is UNCHANGED
//    by this round — it was already the upstream construct, and the 2026-09-02y split
//    note below still holds.
// ── ROOT RE-CHECKED, with a one-variable pair on THIS program, measured 2026-09-07:
//      c.push(&mut y);  c.push(&mut y);                     -> REFUSED
//         "cannot borrow 'y' as mutable: already mutably borrowed"
//      c.push(Box::new(|| { y = 0i64; })) twice              -> ADMITS
//    Only the loan's MINTING SITE differs. So the conflict check is live and reachable;
//    a capture that mutably borrows an upvar deposits no loan in the enclosing body.
//    Same root as issue-58776-borrowck-scans-children (a loan crossing the closure
//    boundary deposits nothing), second door — the outward direction.
// split 2026-09-02y: the port's `Box<dyn FnMut()>` slots are 'static objects and the two
// closures borrow a local — refused by the object-lifetime bound by itself
// (../../fail/borrowck/mut-borrow-conflict-in-closures-vec); this variant bounds the
// objects with `+ '_` and keeps ONLY the upstream defect, the two closures mutably
// borrowing `y` at once through the boxed slots.
// Original path: tests/ui/borrowck/mut-borrow-conflict-in-closures-vec.rs
// upstream commit: 4b0c9d76ae7d387229caea55cfa73c280b08b8a7
// upstream construct: lines 5-9, `fn main` —
//     let mut y = 1;
//     let c = RefCell::new(vec![]);
//     c.push(Box::new(|| y = 0));
//     c.push(Box::new(|| y = 0));
//     //~^ ERROR cannot borrow `y` as mutable more than once at a time
package mut_borrow_conflict_in_closures_vec_bounded;
use logos.mem.boxed;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut y: i64 = 1i64;
    let mut c: Vec<Box<dyn FnMut() + '_>> = Vec::<Box<dyn FnMut() + '_>>::new();
    c.push(Box::new(|| { y = 0i64; }));
    c.push(Box::new(|| { y = 0i64; }));
    return 0i32;
}
